@startuml
title SMS OTP login (request → verify → session)

actor Client
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB
participant "Telnyx (SMS)" as SMS

' Same flow serves the client app (/v1/auth) and the BO (/bo/v1/auth);
' only authorization differs downstream (ADR 0002 & 0004).

== Bootstrap CSRF ==
Client -> FE : open login
FE -> NGINX : GET /v1/auth/csrf/
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.views.CsrfView (@ensure_csrf_cookie)
  AuthN: none (AllowAny)
end note
BE --> FE : 200 + Set-Cookie: csrftoken

== Request code ==
Client -> FE : submit msisdn
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/auth/otp/request
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.serializers.OtpRequestSerializer.validate (E.164)
  Throttle: ScopedRateThrottle "otp" (per IP)
end note
BE -> BE : services.request_otp()
note over BE
  Business rules:
  - per-msisdn rate limit (cooldown + hourly cap)
  - login: account must exist and be active
  - signup: no account may exist yet
  - generate code, store only HMAC-SHA256 hash, TTL ~5 min
end note
BE -> DB : INSERT otp_code (code_hash, expires_at)
BE -> SMS : send_sms(msisdn, code)
note right of SMS
  integrations.telnyx.client.send_sms (OTP is SMS-only — ADR 0007)
  Dev: logs the code when Telnyx is unconfigured
end note
BE --> FE : 200 {"detail": "...code sent"}

== Verify code & open session ==
Client -> FE : submit code (+ profile fields on signup)
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/auth/otp/verify
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.serializers.OtpVerifySerializer.validate
  (signup requires first/last name, email, birthday)
end note
BE -> BE : services.verify_otp()
note over BE
  Business rules (locked row):
  - latest unconsumed code; not expired; attempts < cap
  - constant-time hash compare; wrong code increments attempts (committed)
  - on success mark consumed_at (single-use)
  - login → return user; signup → create_client()
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (otp_code)
BE -> DB : UPDATE otp_code (attempts / consumed_at)
alt signup
  BE -> DB : INSERT users_user (role=client, unusable password)
end
BE -> BE : django.contrib.auth.login(user) — establish session
BE -> DB : INSERT django_session
BE --> FE : 200 (UserSerializer) + Set-Cookie: sessionid (HttpOnly)
FE --> Client : logged in

== Authenticated calls ==
Client -> FE : use app
FE -> NGINX : GET /v1/auth/me (Cookie: sessionid)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  users.views.CurrentUserView
  AuthN: SessionAuthentication; permission IsAuthenticated
end note
BE --> FE : 200 (current user)

note over Client, DB
  Logout: POST /v1/auth/logout (IsAuthenticated) — sends X-CSRFToken,
  clears the server-side session for instant revocation.
end note
@enduml
